<quiz>
  <question type="category">
    <category>
      <text>$course$/ALG2/Units/Unit 01/Lesson 07/ALG2_U01_L07_GuidedPractice</text>
    </category>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U01_L07_GP01</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ALG2_U01_L07_GP01</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.A2.AE.4; MLA.A2.PF.7</p><p>A rectangle has width x and length x + 5. Its area is 84. Which equation models the situation?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[x(x + 5) = 84]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Correct. Area is width times length, so x(x + 5) = 84.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[x + x + 5 = 84]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This models perimeter-like addition, not area.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[x(x - 5) = 84]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[The length is x + 5, not x - 5.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[x + 5 = 84]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This uses only the length expression, not the area relationship.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U01_L07_GP02</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ALG2_U01_L07_GP02</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.A2.AE.4; MLA.A2.PF.7</p><p>Solve x(x + 5) = 84 and choose the reasonable rectangle width.</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[x = -12]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This is an algebraic solution, but a width cannot be negative.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[x = 12]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This is the length when x = 7, not the width.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[x = 7]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Correct. The equation gives x = 7 or x = -12, and only 7 is a reasonable width.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[x = 84]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This is the area, not the width.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U01_L07_GP03</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ALG2_U01_L07_GP03</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.A2.AE.4; MLA.A2.PF.7</p><p>The height model h(t) = -16t&#178; + 64t equals 0 at t = 0 and t = 4. What does t = 4 represent?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[The object starts on the ground.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[That describes t = 0.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[The object returns to the ground after 4 seconds.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Correct. h(t) = 0 means height is zero, and t = 4 is the later time.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[The maximum height is 4 feet.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[The solution t = 4 is a time, not a height.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[The object is 64 feet high after 4 seconds.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[At t = 4, the height is 0.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U01_L07_GP04</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ALG2_U01_L07_GP04</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.A2.AE.4; MLA.A2.PF.7</p><p>A volume model is V(x) = x&#179; + 2x&#178; - 8x. Which positive solution makes V(x) = 0?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[x = -4]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This solves the equation but is not positive.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[x = 0]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This solves the equation but is not a positive dimension.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[x = 8]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This comes from the coefficient, not from solving the equation.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[x = 2]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Correct. Factoring gives x(x + 4)(x - 2) = 0, and the positive solution is 2.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U01_L07_GP05</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ALG2_U01_L07_GP05</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.A2.AE.4; MLA.A2.PF.7</p><p>Why should x = -5 be rejected as a design measurement?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[It is not a real number.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Negative numbers are real numbers.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[A measurement cannot be negative in this context.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Correct. Context determines whether an algebraic solution is reasonable.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[It makes every equation false.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[A rejected contextual solution may still solve the algebraic equation.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[It is larger than the positive solution.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[The issue is that the measurement is negative.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
</quiz>